SUMMARY:Our Journeys\, exhibition opening
DESCRIPTION:Come celebrate the kick-off of AAPI Heritage Month with Our Journeys\, a traveling exhibit presented by Vietnamese Boat People Podcast \nHosted by @Montclair Public Library\n50 South Fullerton Ave\, Montclair\, NJ 07042\n🗓️ Opening Reception: Wednesday\, May 6\n🕠 5:30 – 7:30 PM\nFree! RSVP Required: https://bit.ly/OurJourneysNJ\nDelicious Vietnamese bites by Bánh Voyage! \nExplore:\n• Personal refugee stories that honor journeys of migration\, displacement and finding home\n• An interactive map to plot your ancestors’ migration across generations\n• Community connections with shared histories during AAPI Heritage Month \nPlease note: This exhibition contains themes related to war and displacement that may not be suitable for all audiences. Parental discretion is advised.\nThe exhibit will be on view from May 6 to June 6 during library public hours. https://www.vietnameseboatpeople.org/exhibition \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
