SUMMARY:Big Mamou live at Montclair Brewery
DESCRIPTION:Big Mamou plays a rocking mix of original and traditional Blues\, Country\, Zydeco\, Cajun and New Orleans R&B/Mardi Gras music. Fronted by accordionist/singer\, John Sherman\, and singer Julianne Fenhagen\, Big Mamou also includes guitarist/pedal steel player\, Michael Levine\, upright bassist/vocals\, Jim Fenhagen\, drummer Billy Loos\, keyboards/acoustic guitar Steve Skinner and trombonist/vocals\, Fred Parcells. John was previously in “Jolie Blonde” and toured with legendary guitarist\, Richard Thompson. Julianne was formally with Walter Egan’s band\, “The Wild Ponies” and has performed with Larry Campbell. \n$5 cover charge per person that goes directly to the artists. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
