SUMMARY:AUTHOR TALK: Xochitl Gonzalez 'Last Night in Brooklyn'
DESCRIPTION:The Montclair Literary Festival welcomes bestselling author Xochitl Gonzalez as she talks about her new book Last Night in Brooklyn\, a captivating story about a young woman whose life becomes ensnared in her glamorous neighbor’s secret past. \nA Most Anticipated Book of 2026 from TIME • Oprah Daily • USA Today • People • Harper’s Bazaar • Lit Hub • Book Riot • Publisher’s Weekly • She Reads \nYou will not want to miss this event at 12:30pm on Saturday\, May 9\, 2026\, when the Montclair Literary Festival hosts Xochitl Gonzalez in conversation with Cleyvis Natera\, author of The Grand Paloma Resort. \nTickets to hear Xochitl in person are $35 and include a copy of Last Night in Brooklyn. Xochitl will be signing books after the event. \nThe event will be held at the Student Center Ballroom\, Montclair State University\, 1 Normal Ave\, Montclair. Free parking available at the Red Hawk parking deck. \nBuy tickets here bit.ly/MLF-Brooklyn. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
