SUMMARY:AUTHOR TALK: Maria Semple 'Go Gentle'
DESCRIPTION:The Montclair Literary Festival welcomes Maria Semple\, bestselling author of Where’d You Go\, Bernadette\, as she returns with her most exuberant and life-affirming novel yet. \nGo Gentle is the story of one woman’s cheerful determination to live a life of the mind only to have the heart force its way in. \nA Most Anticipated Book of 2026 from The New York Times • The Washington Post • Harper’s Bazaar • TIME • BBC • Parade • Seattle Times • Lit Hub • Book Riot • Booklist \nYou will not want to miss this event at 5:30pm on Saturday\, May 9\, 2026\, when the Montclair Literary Festival hosts Maria Semple in conversation with Marcy Dermansky\, author of Bad Marie and Hot Air. \nTickets to hear Maria in person are $35 and include a copy of Go Gentle. Maria will be signing books after the event. \nThe event will be held at the Student Center Ballroom\, Montclair State University\, 1 Normal Ave\, Montclair. Free parking available at the Red Hawk parking deck. \nBuy tickets here bit.ly/MLF-Gentle. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/author-talk-maria-semple-go-gentle/
